    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Sport-Management_R-098080-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Sport Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Associate Professor, Sport Management Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department COEHD-Kinesiology Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Kinesiology in the College of Education and Human Development at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor of Sport Management to begin Fall 2027 (rank will be determined upon qualifications). The position is a 3x3 teaching load (2x3 for the first year). Primary teaching responsibilities will consist of undergraduate courses in Sport Management. The position is a full-time, 9-month appointment that will require teaching, scholarly activity and grantsmanship, service, and student mentorship/advisement. More information about the Department of Kinesiology can be found at: https://www.tamucc.edu/education/departments/kinesiology/   Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. State-of-the-art classroom and laboratory buildings, support facilities, and recognized faculty strategically position TAMU-CC to achieve its goal of national and international prominence. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution. The university also proudly competes in NCAA Division I athletics, offering students a dynamic educational experience that combines academic excellence, research, and campus life.   Required Qualifications:   Assistant Rank: Earned doctorate degree in Sport Management or related field. Advanced ABD will be considered; degree must be conferred by the time of appointment Demonstrated evidence of scholarly activity, or evidence of emerging scholarly activity Demonstrated evidence of teaching excellence, or evidence of emerging teaching excellence Experience and/or training in utilizing technology for course delivery (e.g., learning management system, online pedagogy).   Associate Rank: Earned doctorate degree in Sport Management or related field Five (5) years of full-time university faculty experience including at least four (4) years in the rank of Assistant Professor. Related professional experience may substitute in rare cases Demonstrated evidence of scholarly activity, or evidence of emerging scholarly activity Demonstrated evidence of teaching excellence, or evidence of emerging teaching excellence Experience in utilizing technology for course delivery (e.g., learning management system, online pedagogy).     Preferred Qualifications for EITHER RANK : Two (2) or more years of experience teaching undergraduate/graduate sport management courses Effectively teach in a variety of sport management courses, in both the in-person and online modalities Evidence of high-quality teaching, student mentorship and engagement Active research agenda in sport management with demonstrated ability to publish in high-quality, high-impact, peer-reviewed journals Documented success in securing funding Experience advising and mentoring students        Demonstrated commitment to service at both the institutional and professional levels. Relevant industry experience with a professional network of contacts.   TO APPLY : https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php     All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position.   A completed application will include: Letter of application addressing the listed qualifications Curriculum vitae Statement of scholarly activity/research statement (maximum length of 2 pages) Teaching statement (maximum length of 2 pages) A list of three professional references including names, title, phone numbers, and email addresses (which will be contacted if selected as a finalist) Optional: evidence of research proficiency (e.g., 1-2 selected re-prints) and/or evidence of teaching excellence (e.g., selected teaching evaluations, course syllabi) .     Application Deadline: November 15th, 2026 Position Start Date: Fall 2027   For further information contact Search Committee Chair and Program Director: Dr. KC Mayer: (361) 825-6076; kurt.mayer@tamucc.edu .     NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026.   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor--Studio-Art--Photography-_R-097995-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Studio Art (Photography)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor, Studio Art (Photography) Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department School of Arts, Media, & Communication Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Art & Design at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi invites applications for a full-time, 9-month tenure track position at the rank of  Assistant Professor of Studio Art (Photography) to begin Fall 2027. The Department seeks a motivated and collaborative educator and practicing artist with expertise in digital and analogue photography who is enthusiastic about teaching at a student-centered university. Candidates must demonstrate  a record of research, scholarly and/or creative activity, college-level teaching experience, and a commitment to engaging in service activity with university and professional communities.  Upon appointment, the teaching load will consist of 2 courses per semester, with one 3-course semester every two years. This load includes release time for research, scholarly, and/or creative activity.   Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate photography courses, participating in departmental meetings, and contributing to BFA and MFA reviews. Additional studio responsibilities involve managing the photo labs, including overseeing facilities and equipment, purchasing supplies, implementing training and safety protocols, and supervising student workers.   About the Department The Department of Art & Design is committed to cross-disciplinary and collaborative initiatives, fostering community engagement, and mentoring students to become professionally driven artists, designers, scholars, and creative leaders. The department offers the following degrees: Bachelor of Fine Arts in Communication Design, Bachelor of Arts in Art, Bachelor of Fine Arts in Art, Bachelor of Fine Arts with Teacher Certification, and Master of Fine Arts. Exhibition spaces include the Weil Gallery, located in the Center for the Arts building on campus, and the Larry Urban Gallery at 223 N. Chaparral Street. The university’s location also provides convenient access to the metropolitan centers of Houston, San Antonio, Austin, and the Rio-Grande Valley expanding opportunities for cultural engagement. The successful candidate will demonstrate the potential to develop curriculum and instructional strategies that prepare students for advanced studies, and in pursuit of a range of art or art-related opportunities within the region and beyond.   About the University Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications:  Master of Fine Arts with demonstrated expertise in Photography Evidence of active exhibition record demonstrating a sustained creative research practice Evidence of effective teaching at the university or college level   Demonstrated expertise in teaching analogue and digital photography courses (undergraduate and graduate levels) Knowledge of current safety and health standards in photography lab spaces Experience collaborating in a team-oriented work environment    Preferred Qualifications:  Experience with mentoring and providing leadership to undergraduate and graduate students across disciplines  Knowledge of trends and demonstrable expertise in the history, theory, and contemporary field of photography  At least 3 years of teaching experience beyond graduate school   TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position.   A completed application will include: Letter of Interest Teaching Philosophy (single page) Research Statement (single page) Scholarly/Creative Research Activity Statement Curriculum Vitae  A PDF file with twenty images of personal work and/or a link to an online portfolio  A PDF file with twenty images of student work with brief descriptions of assignments, course titles, and years completed Three professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email Unofficial transcripts   Application deadline: Thursday, December 31st, 2026 Position start date: Fall 2027   For more information, contact the Interim Chair of the Department of Art & Design, Michael Sollitto (Michael.sollitto@tamucc.edu), or Committee Chair, Assistant Professor - Art, Jennifer Arnold (jennifer.arnold@tamucc.edu) NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor--Chemistry_R-097979-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor, Chemistry Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Science - Chemistry and BioChemistry Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Texas A&M University–Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track position in Chemistry at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin Fall 2027. The search is broadly focused on organic and physical chemistry, and applications are encouraged from candidates working across a wide range of subdisciplines. We welcome experimental, computational, and theoretical approaches, as well as research that bridges organic and physical chemistry.   The successful candidate will be expected to develop vigorous, externally funded research programs involving both graduate (MS) and undergraduate students. They will also be expected to teach both introductory and advanced courses at the graduate and undergraduate levels in chemistry and other labs and courses as needed. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in service at the university, state, and national level, mentor undergraduate and graduate students, and other duties as assigned. The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry offers both undergraduate and graduate (MS) degrees in chemistry with undergraduate degree tracks in General Chemistry, Biochemistry, Environmental Chemistry, and Physical Science Education Chemistry.   Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. State-of-the-art classroom and laboratory buildings, support facilities, and recognized faculty strategically position TAMU-CC to achieve its goal of national and international prominence. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Chemistry or a closely related field. Evidence of scholarly activity including peer-reviewed publications in leading journals in the field. Strong oral and written communication skills for teaching and scholarship   Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral experience University-level teaching experience is highly desirable   TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the positions.   A completed application will include: A letter of application addressing the listed qualifications A description of research plans including plans for funding support plus a general description of expected start-up support including infrastructure needs. (5 pages max) A statement of teaching philosophy, experience, and interests (3 pages max) A statement of scholarly activity A current and detailed curriculum vitae Copies of unofficial graduate coursework transcripts  Contact information for three professional references including names, addresses, titles, phone numbers, and email addresses   Salary: $7,777.78 - $8,555.56 Approx. Monthly ($70,000- $77,000.04 Approximately annual)   Application Deadline: February 15th, 2027 Position Start Date: Fall 2027   For more information, please contact: Dr. Ben Karimi, Chair of the search committee, Ben.karimi@tamucc.edu   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
