    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-English--Writing-Studies_R-097131-2": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of English, Writing Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Associate Professor of English, Writing Studies Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Liberal Arts Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of English at Texas A&M University–Corpus Christi invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track faculty position in Rhetoric and Composition, beginning Fall 2027. The appointment may be made at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications, level of expertise, and professional experience. The department is seeking an experienced writing program administrator to support the First-Year Writing Program. Applicants should demonstrate a record of excellent teaching and have an active, current scholarly agenda in writing program administration. Teaching expectations will include a 3/3 course load (not including course release time for program administration) comprising first-year writing courses and upper-division undergraduate courses in writing studies. Candidates will also have the opportunity to offer graduate courses and mentor students in the department’s English MA program.  Administrative duties, when part of the faculty’s appointment, will include development and assessment of writing curricula and outcomes and initiating faculty development opportunities to support writing pedagogy in the program. The Department of English offers undergraduate English majors a choice in either a Writing or Literary Studies emphasis, curricula for secondary English certification, certificates in Writing for Non-Profits, social media, and TESOL, and minors in Technical and Professional Writing, Creative Writing, and Literary Studies. The graduate program provides an interdisciplinary educational experience in a generalist MA in English by requiring advanced study in Writing Studies, Literary Studies, and Applied Linguistics. At TAMU-CC, our first-year writing program is informed by research on how people write, how they learn, and what they need to be flexible, adept writers ready to take on new challenges. Our program works to teach writing in ways that connect students to their majors and coordinate with the demands of other first-year classes. As a program, we want to help students understand that writing, language, and rhetoric are all multifaceted and evolving; we want students to be able to use writing and language in ways that will help them achieve their goals. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. The only university in the nation is located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution. Required Qualifications: Assistant Rank: Doctoral degree in Rhetoric and Composition, Writing Studies or related discipline.    Record of active scholarly production or research in, or related to, writing program administration. Record of quality teaching in one or more of the following: Writing Studies, First-Year Writing, and/or Technical and Professional Writing. Demonstrated experience in writing program administration. Associate Rank: Doctoral degree in Rhetoric and Composition, Writing Studies or related discipline.  Record of active scholarly production or research in, or related to, writing program administration. Record of quality teaching in one or more of the following: Writing Studies, First-Year Writing, and/or Technical and Professional Writing.   Five (5) years of full-time university faculty experience including at least four (4) years in the rank of assistant professor. Related professional experience may substitute in rare cases. Demonstrated experience in writing program administration. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated evidence of culturally responsive pedagogy, especially in the context of a regional university designated as a Hispanic-Serving Institution Demonstrated evidence of an ability to teach in face-to-face and online modalities Experience teaching and advising first-generation students and historically underserved communities. Experience in establishing and assessing writing program outcomes TO APPLY : https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A letter of interest addressing qualifications listed, including research agenda and teaching philosophy; A statement of writing program administration philosophy; A current curriculum vitae. Unofficial copies of transcripts of graduate coursework. Three professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses. Candidates whose applications are selected for further review may be asked to provide additional application materials, including a research statement, sample syllabus for a first-year writing course, and writing samples. Application deadline: November 1st, 2026 Position start date: Fall 2027 For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Christopher Andrews, Department Chair, at christopher.andrews@tamucc.edu . NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Math-STEM-Education_R-097804-2": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Math/STEM Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Associate Professor, Math/STEM Education Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Education and Human Development Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education and Human Development invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics/STEM Education to begin Fall 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate educator preparation through high-quality teaching, active research and scholarly agenda in mathematics education, and service to the department, college, university, and profession. Responsibilities include teaching courses in mathematics education and related areas, mentoring students, contributing to program development, and establishing a productive research agenda that includes scholarly publications, presentations, and pursuit of external funding, as appropriate. Candidates should have demonstrated commitment to effective mathematics teaching and learning, collaboration with educational partners, and the university’s teaching, research, and service missions.   The department of Curriculum Instruction and Learning Sciences (CILS) offers the following top-rated academic programs: bachelor of science in early childhood education (EC-3), elementary education (with specializations in bilingual, elementary generalist, and mathematics 4-8), and special education; post baccalaureate  alternative certification; master’s in  curriculum and instruction, elementary education, instructional design and educational technology, reading, secondary education, and special education; and a doctoral degree in curriculum and instruction (with specializations in literacy studies, curriculum studies, instructional design and educational technology, kinesiology, and special education). For more information about the Curriculum, Instruction, and Learning Science department, please visit: https://www.tamucc.edu/education/departments/cils/index.php .   Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. State-of-the-art classroom and laboratory buildings, support facilities, and recognized faculty strategically position TAMU-CC to achieve its goal of national and international prominence. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications :   Assistant Rank: Earned Doctoral degree in Mathematics Education, or a closely related field. Advanced ABD will be considered; degree must be conferred by the time of appointment. A minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Mathematics Education or a closely related area. Three (3) years (EC-12) teaching experience in mathematics education with certification.  Familiarity with educator preparation and certification standards. Evidence of an Emerging Research Record. Associate Rank: Earned Doctoral degree in Mathematics Education, or a closely related field A minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Mathematics Education or a closely related area. Three (3) years (EC-12) teaching experience in mathematics education with certification.  Five (5) years of full-time university faculty experience including at least four (4) years in the rank of assistant professor.   Familiarity with educator preparation and certification standards. Evidence of an Emerging Research Record. Demonstrated experience teaching, mentoring, supervising, or advising students at the university level. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level.   Preferred Qualifications for both Ranks: Membership and active involvement in professional organizations. Demonstrated record of scholarly research and publication in mathematics education/STEM. Demonstrated experience and potential for success in grant writing and securing external funding. Demonstrated experience mentoring doctoral students, including serving on or chairing dissertation committees. Demonstrated experience with instructional technology and online course development. Ability to contribute to undergraduate and graduate programs within the department.  Commitment to student success, collaboration, and service to the department, college, university, and profession.   TO APPLY:  https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position.   A completed application will include: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed. A curriculum vitae. A statement of scholarly activity. A statement of research and teaching philosophy. Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework. A list of three (3) professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email address.   Application Deadline: December 1st, 2026 Position Start Date: Fall 2027   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026.     All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor--Science-Education_R-097805-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Science Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor, Science Education Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department Curriculum Instruction and Learning Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education and Human Development invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Science Education to begin Fall 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate educator preparation through high-quality teaching, an active research and scholarly agenda in science education, and service to the department, college, university, and profession. Responsibilities include teaching courses in science education and related areas, mentoring students, contributing to program development, and establishing a productive research agenda that includes scholarly publications, presentations, and pursuit of external funding, as appropriate. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to effective science teaching and learning, collaboration with educational partners, and the university’s teaching, research, and service missions. The department of Curriculum Instruction and Learning Sciences (CILS) offers the following top-rated academic programs: bachelor of science in early childhood education (EC-3), elementary education (with specializations in bilingual, elementary generalist, and mathematics 4-8), and special education; post baccalaureate  alternative certification; master’s in  curriculum and instruction, elementary education, instructional design and educational technology, reading, secondary education, and special education; and a doctoral degree in curriculum and instruction (with specializations in literacy studies, curriculum studies, instructional design and educational technology, kinesiology, and special education). For more information about the Curriculum, Instruction, and Learning Science department, please visit: https://www.tamucc.edu/education/departments/cils/index.php . Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. Required Qualifications : Earned Doctoral degree in Science Education, Curriculum & Instruction with an emphasis in Science Education, or a closely related field. Advanced ABD will be considered; degree must be conferred by the time of appointment. A minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Science Education or a closely related area. Familiarity with educator preparation and certification standards. Evidence of an Emerging Research Record.   Preferred Qualifications Three (3) years or more of (PK-12) science teaching experience. Membership and active involvement in professional organizations. Demonstrated record of scholarly research and publication in science education. Demonstrated experience teaching, mentoring, supervising, or advising students at the university level. Demonstrated experience with instructional technology and online course development. Ability to contribute to undergraduate and graduate programs within the department. Commitment to student success, collaboration, and service to the department, college, university, and profession. TO APPLY:  https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed. A curriculum vitae. A statement of research and teaching philosophy. A statement of scholarly activity. Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework. A list of three (3) professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email address. Application Deadline: December 1st, 2026 Position Start Date: Fall 2027 NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026.   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
