    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Business-Economics_R-097564-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business Economics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Business Economics Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Business Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Decision Sciences and Economics at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a full-time 9-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Business Economics position beginning Fall 2027. We seek a scholar to teach undergraduate and graduate courses and help launch our new AI-integrated business curriculum. The successful candidate will apply economics, econometrics, data analytics, and emerging AI technologies to business and economic problems. Accredited in both business and accounting by AACSB International, the TAMU-CC College of Business serves a varied student body on the Corpus Christi Island Campus, the RELLIS Campus (Brazos Valley), and online.  The College's values of excellence, integrity, leadership, and sustainability create an attractive environment for faculty from various backgrounds.  Please visit https://www.tamucc.edu/business/ for more information about the College and the University. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast.   Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Economics in a variety of instructional modalities. Contribute to the development and implementation of the College’s AI-integrated curriculum, including Applied Machine Learning for Business, AI Strategy, and Generative AI prototyping. Incorporate appropriate applications of predictive modeling, machine learning, Generative AI, and other emerging technologies into teaching and experiential learning. Conduct high-quality research in the candidate’s field(s). Contribute to the department, college, university, and broader academic and professional communities through appropriate service activities.   Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in Economics or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited (or equivalent) institution. Advanced ABD candidates will be considered; the degree must be conferred at the time of appointment. Demonstrated experience teaching Economics and/or closely related business subjects. Demonstrated record of scholarly research and publication in accordance with faculty qualifications.   Preferred Qualifications Ability to teach courses involving Data Analytics, Econometrics, Machine Learning, or applications of AI to business and economics. Evidence of integrating emerging technologies or data-driven approaches with regard to teaching. High-quality research relating to AI and/or machine learning in Economics   TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: Cover letter outlining qualifications and specific interest in the position, including experience or interest in integrating AI and data analytics with Economics and/or business education. Curriculum Vitae. Scholarly activity statement. Job market research paper in economics Statement of teaching philosophy, including a description of any use of emerging technologies or data-driven approaches in teaching Evidence of teaching excellence, preferably samples of teaching evaluations. Three supervisory professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email address. Unofficial copies of transcripts of graduate coursework.   Salary: Up to $13,333.34 Approx. Monthly (Up to $120,000 Approximately annual)   Application deadline: November 30th, 2026 Position start date: Fall 2027 For questions about the position, contact Dr. Ahmed Kamara, Department Chair, Department of Decision Sciences and Economics, at ahmed.kamara@tamucc.edu . NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor--Civil-Engineering_R-097621-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor, Civil Engineering Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Engineering - ENGR Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Engineering in the College of Engineering and Computer Science at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a 9-month , tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering in the area of transportation engineering to begin Fall 2027 .  The successful candidate will be expected to lead in the continued development of the Bachelor of Science Program in Civil Engineering at TAMU-CC, including curriculum development and refinement and teaching undergraduate engineering courses, to develop a research program in the applicant’s discipline of study, and to mentoring students. The successful candidate will also be expected to assist in the continued development of the program for the Master of Science in Engineering and to contribute to the development of the recently-approved program for the Ph.D. in Engineering.    The Department of Engineering prepares well-educated, highly skilled, and socially and professionally responsible engineers and engineering technologists from various populations of students so that they can have productive and rewarding careers at local, state and national levels. Graduates will be well grounded in the fundamentals of engineering, mathematics, science, communications, and problem solving. To ensure that our graduates are valued by industry and to continually improve our program, input is sought from employers, our alumni and an industry advisory committee so that the changing needs of industry are met.  The Department of Engineering offers programs leading to Bachelor of Science degrees in civil engineering, electrical engineering, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, and mechanical engineering technology.  Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. State-of-the-art classroom and laboratory buildings, support facilities, and recognized faculty strategically position TAMU-CC to achieve its goal of national and international prominence. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. degree in Civil Engineering or a related field; Advanced ABD will be considered, degree must be conferred by the time of appointment; and An established record of scholarship with significant journal publications commensurate with the candidate's level; and A track record in or interest in research and teaching in transportation / traffic engineering.    Preferred Qualifications: Experience in interdisciplinary research and with government or industrial research laboratories. Registration as a Professional Engineer (PE). Additional interest or experience in the areas of surveying and geomatics engineering.    TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include:   1. A letter of application addressing listed qualifications including a statement of teaching & research philosophy, 2. A curriculum vitae, 3. Three professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses – including a current or previous supervisor, and 4. Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework.   The deadline for applications is November 12, 2026.    For more information, please contact the search chair, Dr. Jian Yu, at Jian.Yu@tamucc.edu .     NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Clinical-Professor--Early-Childhood-Education_R-097803-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor, Early Childhood Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Clinical Professor, Early Childhood Education Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department Curriculum Instruction and Learning Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education and Human Development invites applications for a 9-month, non-tenure track position at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor, Early Childhood to begin Fall 2027. The primary responsibility of the clinical assistant professor will be a teaching line focused on the preparation of future educators and the advancement of high-quality early childhood practice. The successful candidate will be a practitioner-scholar who brings expertise from the field into the university classroom, supporting preservice teachers through coursework, mentorship, and field-based supervision. Rather than emphasizing a research agenda, this position centers on excellence in teaching, clinical practice, and service, including building strong partnerships with schools, families, and communities. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to engaging students in experiential learning, fostering responsive and engaging practices, and contributing to program development and service at the department, college, and university levels.   The department of Curriculum Instruction and Learning Sciences (CILS) offers the following top-rated academic programs: bachelor of science in early childhood education (EC-3), elementary education (with specializations in bilingual, elementary generalist, and mathematics 4-8), and special education; post baccalaureate alternative certification; master’s in curriculum and instruction, elementary education, instructional design and educational technology, reading, secondary education, and special education; and a doctoral degree in curriculum and instruction (with specializations in literacy studies, curriculum studies, instructional design and educational technology, kinesiology, and special education). For more information about the Curriculum, Instruction, and Learning Science department, please visit: https://www.tamucc.edu/education/departments/cils/index.php .   Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. State-of-the-art classroom and laboratory buildings, support facilities, and recognized faculty strategically position TAMU-CC to achieve its goal of national and international prominence. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications : An earned Master’s degree in Early Childhood Education, Curriculum & Instruction or closely related field. Minimum of eighteen (18) graduate credit hours in Early Childhood Education. A strong record of active teaching excellence. Effective leadership and a commitment to undergraduate student success within all programs of the Department. Familiarity with educator certification standards. Experience building and nurturing school-university partnerships. Experience teaching, supervising, and advising students. Experience attracting, supporting, and retaining students from varying backgrounds.   Preferred Qualifications A doctoral or terminal degree in Early Childhood Education, Curriculum & Instruction or closely related field. Three (3) years or more of teaching in early childhood classrooms (PK – 3rd Grade) teaching experience. Demonstrated multifaceted and social justice worldview as evidenced by a professional interest in, and experience working with/advocating for underserved populations. Membership and active involvement in professional organizations. Teaching experience at the undergraduate level. Experience with instructional technology and online course development.   TO APPLY:  https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed. A curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy to include evidence of teaching effectiveness. Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework. A list of three (3) professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email address.   Application Deadline: November 15th, 2026 Position Start Date: Fall 2027 Salary: $Up to 6,666.67 Approx. Monthly (Up to $60,000.03 Approximately annual)   For more information, please contact the search chair, Dr. Mary Harper, at Mary.Harper@tamucc.edu .   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professional-Professor--Mechanical-Engineering_R-097623-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professional Professor, Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professional Professor, Mechanical Engineering Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Engineering - ENGR Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Engineering in the College of Engineering and Computer Science at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a Non-Tenure Track position at the rank of Assistant Professional Professor of Mechanical Engineering to begin Fall 2027 .  Applications from candidates with backgrounds in the mechanical engineering sub-disciplines of solid mechanics, manufacturing processes, mechanical systems design, and/or rigid-body mechanics / dynamical systems analysis are sought. The successful candidate will be expected to teach four to five courses per semester in these areas of the undergraduate mechanical engineering and mechanical engineering technology curricula.  There will be some service responsibilities as well.   The Department of Engineering prepares well-educated, highly skilled, and socially and professionally responsible engineers and engineering technologists from a various population of students so that they can have productive and rewarding careers at local, state and national levels. Graduates will be well grounded in the fundamentals of engineering, mathematics, science, communications, and problem solving. To ensure that our graduates are valued by industry and to continually improve our program, input is sought from employers, our alumni and an industry advisory committee so that the changing needs of industry are met.  The Department of Engineering offers programs leading to Bachelor of Science degrees in civil engineering, electrical engineering, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, and mechanical engineering technology, to Master of Science in Engineering degrees with concentrations in civil, electrical, industrial, and mechanical engineering, and to Ph.D. in Engineering degrees with concentrations in the areas of civil and environmental engineering, electrical engineering and advanced manufacturing, industrial and process engineering, and mechanical and energy engineering.  Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. State-of-the-art classroom and laboratory buildings, support facilities, and recognized faculty strategically position TAMU-CC to achieve its goal of national and international prominence. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field; Advanced ABD will be considered, degree must be conferred by the time of appointment; and A track record in or interest in teaching in such areas as solid mechanics, mechanical systems design, manufacturing processes, and/or rigid-body mechanics / dynamical systems analysis; and At least one (1) year of experience teaching in a university engineering program.    Preferred Qualifications: Research and publications in the areas listed above. At least three years experience teaching in a university engineering program.    TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include:   1. A letter of application addressing listed qualifications including a statement of teaching philosophy, 2. A curriculum vitae, 3. Three professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses – including a current or previous supervisor, and 4. Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework.   The deadline for applications is November 12, 2026.    For more information, please contact the search chair, Dr. Aref Mazloum, at Aref.Mazloum@tamucc.edu .   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Clinical-Professor--Generalist_R-097801-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor, Generalist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Clinical Professor, Generalist Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department Curriculum Instruction and Learning Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education and Human Development invites applications for a 9-month, non-tenure track position at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor, Generalist to begin Fall 2027. The primary responsibility of the clinical assistant professor will be a teaching line focused on the preparation of future educators and the advancement of high-quality early childhood practice. The successful candidate will be a practitioner-scholar who brings expertise from the field into the university classroom, supporting preservice teachers through coursework, mentorship, and field-based supervision. Rather than emphasizing a research agenda, this position centers on excellence in teaching, clinical practice, and service, including building strong partnerships with schools, families, and communities. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to engaging students in experiential learning, fostering responsive and engaging practices, and contributing to program development and service at the department, college, and university levels.   The department of Curriculum Instruction and Learning Sciences (CILS) offers the following top-rated academic programs: bachelor of science in early childhood education (EC-3), elementary education (with specializations in bilingual, elementary generalist, and mathematics 4-8), and special education; post baccalaureate  alternative certification; master’s in  curriculum and instruction, elementary education, instructional design and educational technology, reading, secondary education, and special education; and a doctoral degree in curriculum and instruction (with specializations in literacy studies, curriculum studies, instructional design and educational technology, kinesiology, and special education).   Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution. https://www.tamucc.edu/education/departments/cils/index.php .     Required Qualifications : An earned Master’s degree in Curriculum & Instruction or closely related field. Minimum of eighteen (18) graduate credit hours in a specific field. A strong record of active teaching excellence. Effective leadership and a commitment to undergraduate student success within all programs of the Department. Familiarity with educator certification standards. Experience building and nurturing school-university partnerships. Experience teaching, supervising, and advising students.   Preferred Qualifications A doctoral or terminal degree in Curriculum & Instruction or closely related field. Three (3) years or more of teaching in early childhood classrooms (PK – 6th Grade) teaching experience. Membership and active involvement in professional organizations. Teaching experience at the undergraduate level. Experience with instructional technology and online course development.   TO APPLY:  https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed. A curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy to include evidence of teaching effectiveness. Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework. A list of three (3) professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email address.   Application Deadline: November 15th, 2026 Position Start Date: Fall 2027 Salary:   Salary: Up to $7,055.56 Approx. Monthly (Up to $63,500.04 Approximately annual)   For more information, please contact the search chair, Dr. Mary Harper, at Mary.Harper@tamucc.edu .   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026.     All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
