    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professional-Professor-of-Mathematics_R-097718-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professional Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professional Professor of Mathematics Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Science - Math/Statistics Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Mathematics & Statistics in the College of Science seeks a dynamic colleague committed to fostering teaching excellence and student development in a program that values creativity, collaboration, learner-centered pedagogy, and a sense of belonging. The new faculty member will join a collaborative group of 26 mathematics, statistics, and data science faculty who serve the entire university community. We seek applications for a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure-track Assistant Professional Professor position to begin Spring 2027. Although this is a non-tenure track position, progression in rank to professional associate and professional senior professor position is possible. We are particularly interested in a colleague who has preparation and experience in teaching both lower-level and upper-level undergraduate mathematics and statistics courses. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate mathematics and/or statistics courses, including lower-division and upper-division courses. Contribute to ongoing course development and play a leadership role in common assessment and continuous improvement efforts. Participate in departmental and university service appropriate to a teaching-focused appointment. Support student learning and development through effective teaching, mentoring, and engagement with the various student bodies. Workload: The standard teaching load is 15 credit hours per semester (typically five 3-credit courses), for a total of 30 credit hours over the 9-month academic year, plus related service activities. This is a teaching-focused appointment; research is not required. About the Department The Department of Mathematics & Statistics in the College of Science is committed to service excellence and strives to educate students at the University so that they are prepared to use mathematics intelligently in their chosen fields of study and to understand mathematics as and when it affects their lives and their participation in public affairs. The mathematics program prepares its majors and graduate students for careers in education, science, and commerce, and provides a solid foundation for further study in mathematics. We also strive to serve our community by providing expertise to local schools, industry, and business.   TAMU-CC Mission Statement Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a premier institution of higher education, dedicated to providing an unparalleled commitment to student success, developing professionals and engaged leaders, closing achievement gaps as a Hispanic and Minority Serving Institution, and providing intellectual capital through research, creative activity, and innovation for South Texas, the Gulf, and beyond.   About TAMU-CC Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast.   Required Qualifications: Doctoral in Mathematics, Applied Mathematics, or Statistics. Experience working with different student populations at the college level. Breadth and depth of mathematical knowledge. Demonstrated excellence in teaching general undergraduate mathematics/statistics courses. Demonstrated professionalism, dependability, and commitment to fulfilling shared departmental instructional responsibilities.   Preferred Qualifications: Strong commitment and experience in teaching both lower-level and upper-level undergraduate mathematics/statistics courses. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues in performing service. Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills.   TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A complete application includes: Cover letter describing the qualifications for the position Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Copies of all unofficial graduate transcripts A list of three (3) professional references, including names, titles, phone numbers, and email addresses   Application deadline: November 06, 2026 Position start date: Spring 2027   For questions about the position, contact Dr. Devanayagam Palaniappan, Interim Department Chair, Department of Mathematics & Statistics, at devanayagam.palaniappan@tamucc.edu .   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026.   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Instructor-of-Mathematics_R-097720-2": {
      "title": "Instructor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title Instructor of Mathematics Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Science - Math/Statistics Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Mathematics & Statistics in the College of Science seeks a dynamic colleague committed to fostering teaching excellence and student development in a program that values creativity, collaboration, learner-centered pedagogy, and a sense of belonging. The new faculty member will join a collaborative group of 26 mathematics, statistics, and data science faculty who serve the entire university community. The department currently offers degrees in BS Mathematics, MS in Mathematics, and MS in Statistics. We seek applications for a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure track Instructor position to begin Spring 2027. Although this is a non-tenure track position, progression in rank from Instructor to Senior Instructor position is possible. Responsibilities Teach undergraduate mathematics and/or statistics courses, including developmental math courses. Contribute to ongoing course development and coordination of developmental mathematics courses and Summer Bridge Program. Play a leadership role in common assessment and continuous improvement efforts of lower-level undergraduate mathematics and statistics courses. Participate in departmental and university service appropriate to a teaching-focused appointment. Support student learning and development through effective teaching, mentoring, and engagement with the various student bodies. Workload: The standard teaching load is 15 credit hours per semester (typically five 3-credit courses), for a total of 30 credit hours over the 9-month academic year, plus related service activities. This is a teaching-focused appointment; research is not required. About the Department The Department of Mathematics & Statistics in the College of Science is committed to service excellence and strives to educate students at the University so that they are prepared to use mathematics intelligently in their chosen fields of study and to understand mathematics as and when it affects their lives and their participation in public affairs. The mathematics program prepares its majors and graduate students for careers in education, science, and commerce, and provides a solid foundation for further study in mathematics. We also strive to serve our community by providing expertise to local schools, industry, and business.   TAMU-CC Mission Statement Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a premier institution of higher education, dedicated to providing an unparalleled commitment to student success, developing professionals and engaged leaders, closing achievement gaps as a Hispanic and Minority Serving Institution, and providing intellectual capital through research, creative activity, and innovation for South Texas, the Gulf, and beyond.   About TAMU-CC Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast.   Required Qualifications: Master’s or Doctoral degree in Mathematics or Statistics. Ability and willingness to follow established departmental and course policies, and dedication to meeting shared instructional expectations. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with different student populations at the college level. Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. Experience with Summer Bridge Program Demonstrated professionalism, dependability, and commitment to fulfilling departmental and instructional responsibilities. Demonstrated excellence in teaching undergraduate mathematics and statistics courses, or the potential for effective teaching of such courses. Demonstrate a commitment to and preparation for excellence in teaching lower-level undergraduate mathematics courses. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with colleagues in supporting students’ learning experiences across different sections of the same course. One or more years of teaching Developmental Math courses     TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A complete application includes: A letter of interest describing the qualifications for the position Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Copies of all unofficial graduate transcripts A list of three professional references, including names, titles, phone numbers, and email addresses Application deadline: November 06, 2026 Position start date: Spring 2027 For questions about the position, contact Dr. Devanayagam Palaniappan, Department Chair, Interim Department of Mathematics & Statistics, at devanayagam.palaniappan@tamucc.edu . NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026.   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Full-Professor-of-Clinical-Psychology_R-097139": {
      "title": "Assistant/Full Professor of Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Full Professor of Clinical Psychology Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Liberal Arts Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Psychology and Sociology, at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi, invites applications for two full-time (9-month), tenure-track positions in Clinical Psychology beginning Fall of 2027.  One position is at the rank of Assistant Professor, and the other at the rank of Full Professor (see Required Qualifications for rank requirements). The department offers a Bachelor of Arts in Psychology in both traditional and fully online formats, as well as a Master of Arts in Clinical Psychology. We are seeking Full Professor candidates with doctoral-level program experience, as we are considering the development of a PhD in Clinical Psychology. The Psychology programs are among the largest in the College of Liberal Arts, with approximately 500 majors, 100 minors, and 40 graduate students. We seek applicants with a Ph.D. or Psy.D. in Clinical or Counseling Psychology expected to be conferred by the start of the appointment.  Applicants must be licensed or license eligible as a psychologist in Texas.   Priority will be given to candidates with research experience in clinical psychology.  Successful candidates will be expected to teach clinical psychology courses at the undergraduate and master’s level , which may include courses in psychological assessment, psychopathology, and psychotherapy. There may also be opportunities to develop courses in their area of specialization. Tenure-track faculty carry a standard 3-3 teaching load. TAMU-CC is an R2 University, and the department has an increasing focus on research.  We seek candidates with a record of (or potential for) research productivity, and an interest in pursuing external funding.  The successful candidate’s research activities will include mentoring student research and supervising master’s thesis students in our Clinical Psychology MA program. Individuals considered for this position will also be expected to provide clinical supervision to master’s level students, and actively engage in service to the department, college, university, and profession. The successful candidate should have an understanding of multicultural issues and relevant experience in their applications to pedagogy and clinical practice. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System.  It is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast.  With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bay, TAMU-CC is a first-choice institution. For more information on our programs visit our website at: https://www.tamucc.edu/liberal-arts/departments/psychology-sociology/index.php Required Qualifications: Assistant Rank: Earned Ph.D. or Psy.D. in Clinical Psychology or Counseling Psychology from an APA or CPA accredited program. Advanced ABD will be considered; a degree must be conferred by the time of appointment. Be license eligible as a psychologist in the state of Texas at the time of appointment.   Full Professor Rank: Earned Ph.D. or Psy.D. in Clinical Psychology or Counseling Psychology from an APA or CPA accredited program. Be license eligible as a psychologist in the state of Texas at the time of appointment. To be considered for the Full Professor rank, a minimum of ten (10) years of full-time university faculty experience with a minimum of four (4) years of experience at the associate rank or comparable rank is required. Preferred Qualifications: Licensed as a psychologist, preferably in the state of Texas. Independent Clinical experience or research focused in Clinical Psychology. Experience and/or ability to teach/develop courses at the master’s and undergraduate level. A record of, or potential for, research productivity and a clear research agenda. Interest and/or experience in seeking external funding for research. A record of mentoring students in research and supervising clinical students. TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A complete application will include: A letter of application addressing the qualifications listed and relevant professional experience. A curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts of graduate coursework. A two-to-three-page statement summarizing the candidate’s teaching experience and effectiveness. A two-to-three-page statement summarizing the candidate’s recent research activities, as well as research plans for the near future. Contact information for three professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email address.  References will not be contacted unless selected for further consideration. The job posting will remain open until a finalist has been selected.  Application reviews will begin on October 6, 2026. Questions about the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Miguel Moreno, at 361-825-2205 or miguel.moreno@tamucc.edu . NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Industrial-Engineering_R-097682-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Industrial Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Associate Professor, Industrial Engineering Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Engineering - ENGR Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Engineering in the College of Engineering and Computer Science at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a 9-Month, Tenure-Track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor of Industrial Engineering in the areas of manufacturing and production engineering or supply chain and logistics. Faculty rank and tenure status will be determined upon review of qualifications. Other areas of expertise in industrial engineering will be considered as well.  This position is scheduled to begin with the Fall 2027 semester. The successful candidate will be expected to lead in the continued development of the Bachelor of Science Program in Industrial Engineering at TAMU-CC, including curriculum development and refinement and teaching undergraduate engineering courses, to develop a research program in the applicant’s discipline of study, and to mentoring students. The successful candidate will also be expected to assist in the continued development of the program for the Master of Science in Engineering and to contribute to the development of the recently approved program for the Ph.D. in Engineering.    The Department of Engineering prepares well-educated, highly skilled, and socially and professionally responsible engineers and engineering technologists from various populations of students so that they can have productive and rewarding careers at local, state and national levels. Graduates will be well grounded in the fundamentals of engineering, mathematics, science, communications, and problem solving. To ensure that our graduates are valued by industry and to continually improve our program, input is sought from employers, our alumni and an industry advisory committee so that the changing needs of industry are met.  The Department of Engineering offers programs leading to Bachelor of Science degrees in civil engineering, electrical engineering, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, and mechanical engineering technology.  Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. State-of-the-art classroom and laboratory buildings, support facilities, and recognized faculty strategically position TAMU-CC to achieve its goal of national and international prominence. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications: Assistant Rank: An earned Doctoral Degree in Industrial Engineering or a related field; Advanced ABD will be considered, degree must be conferred by the time of appointment; and An established record of scholarship with significant journal publications commensurate with the candidate's level of experience; and A track record in or interest in research and teaching in either manufacturing and production or supply chain and logistics.    Associate Rank: An earned Doctoral Degree in Industrial Engineering or a related field; and Five (5) years of full-time university faculty experience including at least four (4) years in the rank of Assistant Professor. Related professional experience may substitute in rare cases. An established record of scholarship with significant journal publications commensurate with the candidate's level of experience; and A track record in or interest in research and teaching in either manufacturing and production or supply chain and logistics.    Preferred Qualifications for ALL RANKS : Experience in interdisciplinary research and with government or industrial research laboratories. Additional interest or experience in the area of human-systems interface, over and above experience in the previously identified areas.    TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include:   1. A letter of application addressing listed qualifications including a statement of teaching & research philosophy, 2. A curriculum vitae, 3. Three professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses – including a current or previous supervisor, and 4. Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework.   The deadline for applications is November 12, 2026.    For more information, please contact the search chair, Dr. Pablo Rangel, at Pablo.Rangel@tamucc.edu .   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Mechanical-Engineering_R-097624-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Associate Professor, Mechanical Engineering Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Engineering - ENGR Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Engineering in the College of Engineering and Computer Science at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a 9-Month, Tenure-Track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering to begin Fall 2027 . Faculty rank and tenure status will be determined upon review of qualifications. Applications from candidates with backgrounds in the mechanical engineering sub-disciplines of solid mechanics, manufacturing processes, mechanical systems design, and/or rigid-body mechanics / dynamical systems analysis are sought. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses and develop and refine curriculum in these areas, to mentor students, and to develop a research program in the applicant’s discipline of study. The successful candidate will also be expected to assist in the development of the new Ph.D. in Engineering program.    The Department of Engineering prepares well-educated, highly skilled, and socially and professionally responsible engineers and engineering technologists from various populations of students so that they can have productive and rewarding careers at local, state and national levels. Graduates will be well grounded in the fundamentals of engineering, mathematics, science, communications, and problem solving. To ensure that our graduates are valued by industry and to continually improve our program, input is sought from employers, our alumni and an industry advisory committee so that the changing needs of industry are met.  The Department of Engineering offers programs leading to Bachelor of Science degrees in civil engineering, electrical engineering, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, and mechanical engineering technology, to Master of Science in Engineering degrees with concentrations in civil, electrical, industrial, and mechanical engineering, and to Ph.D. in Engineering degrees with concentrations in the areas of civil and environmental engineering, electrical engineering and advanced manufacturing, industrial and process engineering, and mechanical and energy engineering.  Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. State-of-the-art classroom and laboratory buildings, support facilities, and recognized faculty strategically position TAMU-CC to achieve its goal of national and international prominence. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications: Assistant Rank: An earned Doctoral Degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field; Advanced ABD will be considered, degree must be conferred by the time of appointment; and An established record of scholarship with significant journal publications commensurate with the candidate's level; and A track record in or interest in research and teaching in such areas as solid mechanics, mechanical systems design, manufacturing processes, and/or rigid-body mechanics / dynamical systems analysis.   Associate Rank: An earned Doctoral Degree in Mechanical Engineering or related field. Five (5) years of full-time university faculty experience including at least four (4) years in the rank of Assistant Professor. Related professional experience may substitute in rare cases. An established record of scholarship with significant journal publications commensurate with the candidate's level; and A track record in or interest in research and teaching in such areas as solid mechanics, mechanical systems design, manufacturing processes, and/or rigid-body mechanics / dynamical systems analysis.   Preferred Qualifications for ALL RANKS : Experience in interdisciplinary research and with government or industrial research laboratories.   TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include:   1. A letter of application addressing listed qualifications including a statement of teaching & research philosophy, 2. A curriculum vitae, 3. Three professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses – including a current or previous supervisor, and 4. Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework.   The deadline for applications is November 12, 2026.    For more information, please contact the search chair, Dr. Dugan Um, at Dugan.Um@tamucc.edu .   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Art-in-Sculpture_R-097587": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art in Sculpture",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Art in Sculpture Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department School of Arts, Media, & Communication Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Art & Design at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track, Assistant Professor of Art in Sculpture starting Fall 2027. We seek a motivated, collaborative artist-educator with expertise in three-dimensional art who is passionate about teaching within a student-centered university environment. Candidates should demonstrate an active studio practice, a strong exhibition record, college-level teaching experience, and a commitment to fostering a supportive academic community.   Position Overview As a faculty member in Sculpture, you will teach undergraduate and graduate courses while contributing to the academic and creative growth of students. Responsibilities include: Teaching 3D Foundations and undergraduate and graduate Sculpture courses. Participating in departmental meetings and BFA/MFA reviews. Managing sculpture facilities, equipment, and studio operations. Purchasing supplies and maintaining resources necessary for instruction. Implementing training programs and safety protocols. Contributing to the recruitment, retention, and success of undergraduate BFA students and graduate students in the MFA program. Providing mentorship and guidance to graduate assistants and collaborating with adjunct faculty teaching in the sculpture area. Contributing to a collaborative, cross-disciplinary departmental environment. The teaching load consists of a 2/2/2/3 load, typically teaching two studio art courses each long semester and three studio art courses during one semester in every four-semester cycle   Join Our Creative Community This position offers the opportunity to contribute to a dynamic department that values artistic excellence, innovative teaching, collaborative scholarship, and student success. If you are committed to advancing contemporary sculpture education and mentoring the next generation of artists, we encourage you to apply.   About the Department The Department of Art & Design is dedicated to cross-disciplinary collaboration, community engagement, and mentoring students to become professionally driven artists, designers, scholars, and creative leaders. The department offers undergraduate and graduate degree programs and supports exhibition opportunities through the Weil Gallery on campus and the Larry Urban Gallery in downtown Corpus Christi.   About the University Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications Master of Fine Arts degree with demonstrated expertise in Sculpture/3D art. Evidence of active professional artistic practice and exhibition record. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Ability to teach 3D Foundations and advanced undergraduate and graduate Sculpture courses. Knowledge of current safety and health standards in sculpture studios. Experience working collaboratively with students, faculty, and staff in a team-oriented environment. Commitment to effectively serve and promote a varied student population.   Preferred Qualifications Teaching expertise in areas such as figurative sculpture, woodworking, fabrication, metal casting, mold-making, soft sculpture, or installation. Experience integrating digital fabrication technologies such as 3D scanning and printing into traditional 3D media. Ability to mentor, teach, and provide leadership to graduate students across disciplines. Knowledge of historical, theoretical, and contemporary developments in Sculpture. Leadership experience in studio-based educational settings.   TO APPLY : https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: Letter of Interest or Cover Letter. Teaching Philosophy or Teaching Statement. Curriculum Vitae. Scholarly activity statement. Portfolio consisting of twenty images of personal work and/or a link to an online portfolio. Twenty images of student work labeled with assignment name, a brief description, and course level (beginning, intermediate, advanced, graduate) information. Unofficial copies of transcripts of graduate coursework Three professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses   Application deadline: Thursday, December 31st, 2026 Position start date: Fall 2027   For more information, contact Interim Art Department & Design Chair, Michael Sollitto (Michael.sollitto@tamucc.edu), or Committee Chair, Assistant Professor - Ceramics, Leandra Urrutia (Leandra.urrutia@tamucc.edu)   NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Finance-Financial-Planning_R-097424-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Finance/Financial Planning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Finance/Financial Planning Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Business Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Finance at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi invites applications for a 9-month tenure track, Assistant Professor of Finance, starting in Fall 2027. This position will require a doctoral degree in Financial Planning or Finance from an AACSB-accredited institution. The Department seeks candidates whose academic preparation and teaching interests complement its programs in financial planning education, including preparation for the Certified Financial Planner™ (CFP®) examination. The successful candidate will be expected to teach primarily undergraduate and/or graduate courses that support the financial planning curriculum and prepare students for the CFP® certification examination. Teaching responsibilities may include courses in areas such as principles of financial planning, retirement planning, estate planning, tax planning, insurance and risk management, investment planning, employee benefits, and financial planning capstone. The faculty member should also be prepared to teach other finance courses as needed by the department, including but not limited to corporate finance, investments, financial institutions, personal finance, and related areas. The successful candidate must be able to teach effectively in multiple instructional modalities, including face-to-face, hybrid, online, hyflex, and other formats as assigned by the department. The candidate will also be expected to maintain an active research agenda, contribute to the scholarly mission of the department and the college, advise and mentor students, participate in curriculum development, and provide service to the department, the college, the university, the profession, and the community. Accredited in both business and accounting by AACSB International, the TAMU-CC College of Business serves a varied student body on the Corpus Christi Island Campus, the RELLIS Campus (Brazos Valley), and online.  The College's values of excellence, integrity, leadership, and sustainability create an attractive environment for faculty from various backgrounds.  Please visit https://www.tamucc.edu/business/ for more information about the College and the University.  Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Financial Planning or Finance from an AACSB-accredited institution. Advanced ABD candidates will be considered; the degree must be conferred at the time of appointment. Must have earned the CFP designation or completed all educational requirements necessary to sit for the CFP® exam, which must be passed within 2 years of employment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching courses aligned with CFP® Board educational requirements Relevant finance certifications   Professional and industry experience in finance-related fields. Experience teaching online/hyflex courses Experience teaching graduate courses Engagement with student activities TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A letter of application that clearly demonstrates the applicant’s qualifications, experience, and alignment with the requirements of the position. A current curriculum vitae A statement of research philosophy A statement of teaching philosophy Evidence of CFP® certification or transcripts documenting completion of the coursework required by the CFP Board to sit for the CFP® examination Three professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses Unofficial copies of transcripts of graduate coursework  At least one Official Copy of student evaluations of teaching from within the last 3 years.  Application deadline: December 30th, 2026 Position start date: Fall 2027 For questions about the position, contact Dr. Bland, Professor of Finance and Search Committee Chair, at Eugene.bland@tamucc.edu . NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor--Higher-Education-Aministration_R-097479-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Higher Education Administration",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor, Higher Education Administration Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College of Education and Human Development Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education and Human Development at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi invites applications for a 9-Month, Tenure-Track position of Higher Education Administration at the rank of Assistant Professor in the Department of Educational Leadership. The position may begin as early as the Fall 2027 semester.   The Department of Educational Leadership is committed to advancing educational leadership across all educational settings. We offer five graduate programs of study, including the M.S. in Higher Education Administration and the Ed.D. in Educational Leadership with a concentration in Higher Education Administration. Both emphasize college student development, institutional governance, and operations through a critical justice-oriented lens.   The primary responsibilities of this position include: Teaching graduate-level courses in the Higher Education Administration M.S. and Educational Leadership Ed.D. programs, including core and applied-research topics; Establishing and leading an active research agenda commensurate with a Carnegie Research 2 institution, with an emphasis on producing impactful scholarship and pursuing external funding opportunities; Disseminating research findings through peer-reviewed publications, practitioner outlets, and scholarly conferences; Advising and mentoring graduate students, including chairing and serving on dissertation committees; and Supporting student recruitment and retention in both the M.S. and Ed.D. programs.   We seek a scholar with higher education experience who will help advance the university's mission and prepare future educational leaders. More specifically, we seek a colleague prepared to teach graduate courses in the M.S. in Higher Education Administration and Ed.D. in Educational Leadership programs, particularly in areas such as organization and administration, academic advising and student support, student development, and related areas of higher education practice. The successful candidate will maintain an active research agenda related to higher education leadership, organizations, student success, policy, or institutional practice and contribute to the preparation of graduate students for leadership roles across colleges and universities; and support the continued growth, recruitment, and retention of students in the department’s graduate programs .   Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic- and Minority-Serving Doctoral Research Institution that has proudly maintained a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree-lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail, and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution.   Required Qualifications: Earned doctorate in higher education, higher education leadership or policy, postsecondary education, student affairs administration, or a closely related field; Advanced ABD will be considered, degree must be conferred by the time of appointment. At least three (3) years of full-time professional administrative experience in higher education institutions (e.g., academic advising, student affairs, enrollment management, or student support services) Experience teaching graduate-level coursework in higher education administration, including organization and administration and/or other areas related to academic advising, student support, student development, or institutional practice Demonstrated evidence of engaging in scholarly/creative works and teaching to enhance the mission of the university related to higher education leadership, organizations, student success, and institutional practice Demonstrated participation in scholarly-practitioner communities (e.g., campus, state-wide, and national conferences) and the dissemination of scholarship to both academic and applied audiences   Preferred Qualifications: At least five (5) years of full-time professional administrative experience in higher education institutions Experience contributing to programmatic, organizational, or student-success improvement initiatives in higher education settings Evidence of sustained involvement or leadership in higher education or student-support professional associations through committee service, conference presentations or workshops, or elected or appointed leadership roles Experience contributing to externally funded research or demonstrated potential to pursue external funding Experience teaching and mentoring graduate students from varying backgrounds, including in online or hybrid learning environments, with a demonstrated commitment to supporting student success   TO APPLY: https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php   All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include:   Cover letter that includes: a description of how you meet the qualifications listed, including expertise and scholarly emphasis in area(s) listed (two single-spaced pages limit) A statement of research and teaching philosophy Current Curriculum Vitae Copies of unofficial transcripts of graduate coursework A list of three (3) professional references including names, titles, phone numbers, and email addresses. Review of applications will begin immediately, and the deadline for applications is open until filled.   For more information, please contact the search chair, Dr. Rosie Banda, at rosie.banda@tamucc.edu .     NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor--Kinesiology---Athletic-Training_R-097210-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Kinesiology - Athletic Training",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor, Kinesiology - Athletic Training Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department COEHD-Kinesiology Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education and Human Development invites applications for a full-time , 9-month Tenure-Track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Kinesiology - Athletic Training   to begin as early as Fall 2027 . We are seeking a dynamic faculty member to assist in the continued development of a Commission on Accreditation of Athletic Training Education (CAATE) accredited Athletic Training Program. This position will require teaching, research or creative activity, and service. This position will serve as the third faculty line for the Master of Science in Athletic Training program. The main responsibilities of this position will include, but are not limited to:  Teaching master’s level Athletic Training classes in a CAATE accredited AT Program and maintaining compliance with CAATE accreditation standards Teaching in an accredited graduate Athletic Training program and an undergraduate kinesiology program designed to help students enter allied health professions Academic advising, mentorship, and research supervision for students in a MSAT Program Supporting activities and programs arranged for the recruitment, selection, and retention of students for the MSAT Program Assisting in the completion of necessary annual and self-study accreditation reports for CAATE, SACS-COC, and the university Active engagement in scholarship & creative activity Providing service to the university, community, and profession Additional duties as assigned The successful candidate will report to the Director of the Athletic Training Program and the Chair of the Department of Kinesiology & Military Science.  Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree-lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail, and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution. For more information about the Department of Kinesiology & the Athletic Training Program can be found at: http://kinesiology.tamucc.edu/index.html Required Qualifications : A doctoral degree in Athletic Training, Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Curriculum and Instruction, or applicable field. Advanced ABD will be considered; degree must be conferred at the time of appointment. Proven record of dedicated line of scholarship, including recent active engagement, publications, and/or potential for on-going research and other scholarly and creative activities Proven record in or interest in teaching in athletic training or applicable field. Current Board of Certification (BOC) certification  Current membership in the National Athletic Trainers’ Association (NATA) Proof of NPI number with appropriate health care field designation Eligibility for Texas AT Licensure or Current Texas AT License Documented clinical experience in the field of Athletic Training Preferred Qualifications Documented fundable line of scholarship and/or record of receipt of grants Evidence of successful graduate and/or undergraduate teaching in a CAATE accredited Athletic Training Program (previous 3-5 years) Experience working with the Commission on Accreditation of Athletic Training Education (CAATE) Current knowledge of Athletic Training literature and CAATE requirements   Evidence of outstanding organizational skills; as well as excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills Demonstrated commitment to global competency with the skills and experience to work with individuals from various backgrounds Knowledge and experience concerning Board of Certification (BOC) Approved Provider status CPR/AED/First Aid Professional Rescuer Instructor or BLS Instructor TO APPLY:  https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed A curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy A statement of research philosophy Proof of Current BOC certification Proof of NPI number with appropriate health care field designation Proof of Current NATA Membership Copies of unofficial transcripts for graduate coursework A list of three (3) professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email address Application Deadline: Monday, November 23rd, 2026 Position Start Date: Fall 2027 Salary: $7,127.56 Monthly NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. For more information, please contact the search chair, Dr. Mikaela Boham , at Mikaela.Boham@tamucc.edu . All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Visiting-Assistant-Professor-of-Political-Science_R-097134-1": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nJob Title Visiting Assistant Professor of Political Science Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Liberal Arts Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Liberal Arts is seeking a Visiting Assistant Professor of Political Science in American Politics to begin in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will show excellent and enthusiastic teaching skills and demonstrate the ability to work in a team environment. Course assignments will be undergraduate courses across the Political Science curriculum. Teaching assignments may include classroom (face-to-face), hybrid, and online classes with various class sizes. Candidates should be prepared to teach core curriculum requirements such as American government and state and local government (emphasis on Texas). In addition, candidates will contribute to the teaching needs of the Political Science major including courses such as introduction to political science, Mexican American politics, research methods, and the senior capstone. The normal teaching load will be 4-4. The Department of Social Sciences (DSOC) is a multi-disciplinary department in the College of Liberal Arts that offers undergraduate degrees in Political Science and Criminal Justice and the graduate degree of Master of Public Administration. Through its contribution to the core curriculum, Political Science is one of the largest generators of student credit hours for the university. The Criminal Justice program is one of the largest undergraduate majors on campus. The MPA program is the second largest graduate program in the College of Liberal Arts. DSOC faculty are leaders on campus, in the community, and in their disciplines. We value excellence and work daily to support the University’s Islander Impact 2030 Overarching Goal to be nationally recognized for student success, academic achievement, research, creative activity, innovation, and service excellence. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution. Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Political Science or a closely related discipline from an accredited university. Advanced ABD will be considered; degree must be conferred at the time of appointment.  Ability to teach courses in the Political Science program (including American government, state/Texas and local government, introduction to political science, research methods, and senior capstone).  Ability to teach in a variety of formats and class sizes to include classroom, hybrid, and online courses. Commitment to excellence in teaching and student mentoring. TO APPLY : https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A letter of application addressing qualifications listed above including a teaching philosophy and/or evidence of excellence in teaching A curriculum vitae Three professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses. Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts Application deadline: Sunday, November 1st, 2026 Position start date: Fall 2027 For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Isla Schuchs Carr, Department Chair, at isla.schuchscarr@tamucc.edu . NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-English--Applied-Linguistics_R-096912-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English, Applied Linguistics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of English, Applied Linguistics Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Liberal Arts Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of English at Texas A&M University–Corpus Christi invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of English, with a concentration in Applied Linguistics, beginning in Fall 2027. The position entails a 3/3 teaching load and has commensurate research and service expectations. Summer and online teaching opportunities may be available. The Department of English allows English majors to pursue undergraduate coursework with either a Writing or Literary Studies emphasis. The department additionally offers curricula for secondary English certification; certificates in Writing for Non-Profits, social media, and TESOL; and minors in Technical and Professional Writing, Creative Writing, and Literary Studies. The graduate program provides an interdisciplinary educational experience by requiring coursework in Literary Studies, Writing Studies, and Applied Linguistics.  The Applied Linguistics faculty coordinate and teach the courses for two undergraduate TESOL certificates. In addition, they teach courses in the ENGL BA, ENGL BA with secondary English teaching certification, ENGL MA, Elementary Education BS, and BIEM ESL Minor. The TESOL certificates are pursued by students from across the university with an enrollment of 50+ students. Texas A&M University–Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic-Serving Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. With palm tree-lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail, and a university beach, Texas A&M University–Corpus Christi is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast.   Required Qualifications: A PhD in Applied Linguistics or related field. Advanced ABD will be considered; degree must be conferred at the time of appointment.    Demonstrated a successful research agenda specializing in at least two of the following areas: TESOL methods, technology-assisted language learning/teaching, corpus linguistics, or an area of sociolinguistics. Preferred qualifications: Demonstrated commitment to teaching a broad range of applied linguistics courses at the undergraduate level. Experience teaching language learners. Experience working with first-generation students and historically underserved communities. TO APPLY : https://www.tamucc.edu/human-resources/careers/index.php All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A letter of interest consisting of three distinct parts: (Part 1) Directly addressing the job description; (Part 2) Explicitly presenting a teaching philosophy; and (Part 3) Providing a research statement. A current curriculum vitae Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts Three letters of recommendations Application deadline: Friday , October 23rd, 2026 Position start date: Fall 2027 For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Christopher Andrews, Department Chair, at christopher.andrews@tamucc.edu . NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor--Nursing-Practice_R-096916-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Nursing Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor, Nursing Practice Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Nursing and Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Nursing and Health Sciences (CONHS) at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMUCC) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Nursing Practice beginning Fall 2027. This is a 9-month academic appointment with a possible summer appointment and will be located at the Corpus Christi campus. Faculty members are required to be physically on campus as needed to contribute to academic mission of the College and University. Job Description All tenure and tenure-track positions will have responsibilities in research, teaching, and service missions. Tenure-track faculty are expected to teach students, pursue a robust program of research, seek external funding, and disseminate research findings. Faculty are expected to model exemplar professional behavior through work with students, peers, administration, and community colleagues and to provide student support to include mentoring, advising, recruiting, and DNP student project supervision. Teaching responsibilities ensures adherence to program policies, course objectives, program outcomes and current teaching, clinical, and simulation best practices and safety measures. All faculty are expected to maintain content and clinical mastery, and to participate in college, university and professional service activities. Active participation in college and university committees and activities is required. The faculty members will develop and maintain an active program of scholarship and disseminate scholarly work through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and other appropriate venues. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution. Required Qualifications: Candidates must hold a research focused PhD in Nursing from an accredited institution. While advanced ABD will be considered, degree must be conferred at the time of appointment. Current unencumbered RN and/or APRN License in the State of Texas by the time of appointment. Demonstrated record of high-quality teaching Evidence of leadership capability and ability to work effectively with interprofessional groups. Potential for establishing a program of research and scholarship with a record of successful funding. Preferred Qualifications Post‐ doctoral education/training. Experience coordinating academic nursing programs Experience with classroom/didactic course teaching. Prior experience with baccalaureate and/or graduate nursing education program approvals, national accreditation, online and in-person didactic teaching. Records of professional service at local or national levels. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and with community practice partners. TO APPLY: http://hr.tamucc.edu/careers/ All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A letter of application addressing the qualifications listed and a teaching and research philosophy statement. A current curriculum vitae. Three professional references, including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses- including a previous or current supervisor. Copies of unofficial transcripts for undergraduate and graduate coursework. The job posting will remain open until a finalist is selected. Applications will be reviewed immediately. NOTE:  Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Associate-Professor--Nursing-Practice_R-096918-1": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Nursing Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Associate Professor, Nursing Practice Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Nursing and Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Nursing and Health Sciences (CONHS) at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMUCC) invites applications for a tenure-track Associate Professor of Nursing Practice beginning Fall 2027. This is a 9-month academic appointment with a possible summer appointment and will be located at the Corpus Christi campus. Faculty members are required to be physically on campus as needed to contribute to academic mission of the College and University. Job Description All tenure and tenure-track positions will have responsibilities in research, teaching, and service missions. Tenured/tenure-track faculty are expected to teach students, pursue a robust program of research, seek external funding, and disseminate research findings. Faculty are expected to model exemplar professional behavior through work with students, peers, administration, and community colleagues and to provide student support to include mentoring, advising, recruiting, and DNP student project supervision. Teaching responsibilities ensures adherence to program policies, course objectives, program outcomes and current teaching, clinical, and simulation best practices and safety measures. All faculty are expected to maintain content and clinical mastery, and to participate in college, university and professional service activities. Active participation in college and university committees and activities is required. The faculty members will maintain an active program of scholarship and disseminate scholarly work through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and other appropriate venues. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution. Required Qualifications: Candidates must hold a research focused PhD in Nursing from an accredited institution. Current unencumbered RN and/or APRN License in the State of Texas by the time of appointment. An established program of research and scholarship with a record of successful funding. Experience in higher education including classroom and/or clinical teaching. To be considered for an Associate Professor rank, a minimum of five (5) years of experience at the Assistant Professor or comparable rank is required. Preferred Qualifications Post‐ doctoral education/training. Experience coordinating academic nursing programs Experience in teaching and developing nursing leadership and management courses. Records of professional service at local or national levels. Teaching experience at the graduate level Experience with web-based course delivery, including on-line course development, online teaching, and application of best practices in online education Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and with community practice partners. TO APPLY: http://hr.tamucc.edu/careers/ All required documentation must be uploaded to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A letter of application addressing qualifications listed and a teaching and research philosophy statement. A current curriculum vitae. Three (3) professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses- including a previous or current supervisor. Copies of unofficial transcripts for undergraduate and graduate coursework. The job posting will remain open until a finalist is selected. Applications will be reviewed immediately. NOTE:  Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
