    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Clinical-Professor--Nursing-Practice_R-096919-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor, Nursing Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Clinical Professor, Nursing Practice Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Nursing and Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Nursing and Health Sciences (CONHS) at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing Practice to begin as early as Spring 2027. This is a 9-month academic appointment with a possible summer appointment and will be located at the Corpus Christi campus. Faculty members are required to be physically on campus as needed to contribute to academic mission of the College and University. Job Description The CONHS non-tenure-track faculty responsibilities include teaching, service and implementation and evaluation of nursing courses and student learning. Faculty are expected to model exemplar professional behavior through work with students, peers, and community colleagues and to provide student support to include mentoring, advising, recruiting, FNP student clinical placement, and DNP student project supervision. Faculty are also expected to participate in activities that contribute to achieving TAMU-CC and CONHS organizational goals. Teaching responsibilities include working in collaboration with department chair, program director and program faculty to ensure quality program curriculum and instruction in the didactic and clinical phases of the program. Duties include course management, teaching, skills and simulation labs, student advisement, and student formative and summative evaluation. Responsibilities may also include participation in clinical site visits, scholarly project committee work, student remediation, test writing and analysis, program admissions, accreditation processes and program assessment to include serving on in-person faculty meetings and committees essential to the Family Nurse Practitioner and Doctor of Nursing Practice programs, college, and university’s functioning. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. With palm tree-lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and a university beach, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. Required Qualifications: Master’s in Nursing from an accredited institution. Minimum of two (2) years of clinical nursing experience. Current unencumbered RN License and/or APRN License in the State of Texas or eligible for licensure in Texas at time of hire. Current board certification as an FNP from AANP or ANCC Preferred Qualifications: One to two (1 -2) years of academic teaching experience Earned doctorate in nursing (PhD, DNP) or related field (e.g., EdD) Experience with classroom/didactic course teaching. Knowledge of curriculum and curriculum development. Knowledge of National Organization of Nurse Practitioner Faculties (NONPF) Competencies for nurse practitioners (NPs). Experience in program coordination and management, including curriculum refinement and student progress. Experience with web-based course delivery, including on-line course development, online teaching, and application of best practices in online education. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and with community practice partners. TO APPLY: http://hr.tamucc.edu/careers/ All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A letter of application addressing qualifications listed and a teaching philosophy statement. A current curriculum vitae. Three (3) professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses- including a previous or current supervisor.  Copies of unofficial transcripts for undergraduate and graduate coursework. The job posting will remain open until a finalist is selected. Applications will be reviewed immediately. NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Professor--Healthcare-Administration_R-096910-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Healthcare Administration",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor, Healthcare Administration Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Nursing and Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Nursing and Health Sciences (CONHS) at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor of Health Sciences in Healthcare Administration (HCAD) to begin as early as Fall 2027. This is a 9-month academic appointment with a possible summer appointment and will be located at the Corpus Christi campus. Faculty members are required to be physically on campus as needed to contribute to academic mission of the College and University. Job Description We are seeking candidates with expertise in healthcare administration who demonstrate teaching and/or research expertise across multiple areas relevant to the program, including healthcare information systems, artificial intelligence and emerging technologies in healthcare, project management, health law, and health services research. Tenure-track faculty are expected to teach students, pursue a robust program of research, seek external funding, and disseminate research findings. Faculty are expected to model exemplary professional behavior through work with students, peers, administration, and community colleagues and to provide student support including mentoring, advising, recruiting, and HCAD student project supervision. Teaching responsibilities ensures adherence to program policies, course objectives, program outcomes and current teaching, experiential, and applied learning best practices. All faculty are expected to maintain content expertise, and to participate in college, university and professional service activities. Active participation in College and University committees and activities is required. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate Healthcare Administration courses and, as appropriate, contribute to graduate-level teaching within the College. The faculty member will develop and maintain an active program of scholarship, with scholarly work disseminated through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and other appropriate venues. The successful candidate will foster relationships with healthcare organizations and community partners, support the development of internships and other experiential learning opportunities, contribute to program assessment and continuous improvement, and participate in activities that advance the goals of CONHS and TAMU-CC. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic Serving Doctoral Research Institution with a strong academic reputation, accomplished faculty, and highly regarded degree programs. Since 1947, the University has built a tradition of excellence in teaching, research, innovation, and community engagement as a member of The Texas A&M University System. Located on its own island in the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast, TAMU-CC offers a distinctive learning and working environment surrounded by natural wetlands, scenic trails, beaches, and bays. Required Qualifications A PhD in Healthcare Administration, Health Sciences, or a closely related field relevant to healthcare administration. While advanced ABD will be considered, the degree must be conferred at the time of appointment. Evidence of scholarly activity commensurate with the tenure track expectations of the College and University. Demonstrated capacity to teach undergraduate courses in Healthcare Administration across multiple content areas. Preferred Qualifications At least one (1) year of teaching experience at the baccalaureate and/or graduate level. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues across disciplines and with healthcare organizations and community partners. Evidence of an active or developing program of research, including peer- reviewed scholarly publications and potential for external funding. Experience developing and teaching high -quality online courses. Teaching, research, and/or professional experience across one or more areas of healthcare administration, including healthcare information systems, artificial intelligence and emerging technologies in healthcare, project management, health law, and health services research. Experience supporting student experiential learning through internships, applied projects, or partnerships with healthcare organizations. All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. TO APPLY: http://hr.tamucc.edu/careers A completed application will include: A letter of application addressing the qualifications listed, including a statement of teaching/research philosophy. A curriculum vitae. Three professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses. Copies of unofficial transcripts for undergraduate and graduate coursework. The job posting will remain open until a finalist has been selected. Applicants are encouraged to apply by December 1, 2026 . NOTE:  Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCC_External/job/Corpus-Christi-TX/Assistant-Clinical-Professor-of-Nursing-Education_R-096780-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing Education Agency Texas A&M University - Corpus Christi Department College Of Nursing Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Corpus Christi, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Nursing and Health Sciences (CONHS) at Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi (TAMU-CC) invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing Education to begin as early as Spring 2027. This is a 9-month academic appointment with a possible summer appointment and will be located at the Corpus Christi campus. Faculty members are required to be physically on campus as needed to contribute to academic mission of the College and University. Job Description The CONHS non-tenure-track faculty responsibilities include teaching, service and implementation and evaluation of nursing courses and student learning. Faculty are expected to model exemplar professional behavior through work with students, peers, and community colleagues and to provide student support to include mentoring, advising, recruiting, and BSN prelicensure student clinical placement. Faculty are also expected to participate in activities that contribute to achieving TAMUCC and CONHS organizational goals. Teaching responsibilities include working in collaboration with academic program coordinators, and program faculty to ensure quality program curriculum and instruction in the didactic and clinical phases of the program. Duties include course management, teaching, skills and simulation labs, student advisement, and student formative and summative evaluation. Responsibilities may also include participation in clinical site visits, committee work, student remediation, test writing and analysis, program admissions, accreditation processes and program assessment to include serving on in-person faculty meetings and committees essential to the prelicensure undergraduate nursing programs (BSN), college, and university’s functioning. Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a vibrant, Hispanic and Minority Serving R2 Doctoral Research Institution that proudly provides a solid academic reputation, renowned faculty, and highly rated degree programs since 1947. The University has a heritage of teaching excellence with innovation in research and community engagement as part of the distinguished Texas A&M System. TAMU-CC is the only university in the nation located on its own island, at the heart of the Texas Gulf Coast. With palm tree lined pathways throughout the campus, nearby natural wetlands, a scenic hike-and-bike trail and pristine views of the beach and bays, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi is a first-choice institution. Required Qualifications: Master’s in Nursing from an accredited institution. Minimum of two (2) years of clinical nursing experience. Current unencumbered RN License and/or APRN License in the State of Texas or eligible for licensure in Texas at time of hire. If APRN, current board certification is an FNP is required from AANP or ANCC Preferred Qualifications: One to two (1 -2) years of academic teaching experience Experience with classroom/didactic course teaching or participating in health care simulations. Nursing practice specialty certification (e.g., CNE, RNC-OB, CHSE) Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and with community practice partners. TO APPLY: http://hr.tamucc.edu/careers/ All required documentation must be submitted to be considered for the position. A completed application will include: A letter of application addressing qualifications listed and a teaching philosophy statement. A current curriculum vitae. Three (3) professional references including name, address, title, telephone number, and email addresses- including a previous or current supervisor. Copies of unofficial transcripts for undergraduate and graduate coursework. The job posting will remain open until a finalist is selected. Applications will be reviewed immediately. NOTE: Employment may be impacted by the Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025 and the moratorium issued by Texas Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
